<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>10th Feb</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Final update</B> <P>
<font size="3">

And Wudan draws to an end. <P>

Many thanks to all those who joined and participated in the true spirit of the guild. There are many people both
in the guild an on the old Rallos Zek who played the game how it should be played. Those who enjoyed the escapism, 
the highs/lows and above all made gaming a pleasure not only for themselves but those around them.<P>

It doesn't say much about someone when they can trash talk on message boards, put other people down in a pretty
lame attempt to look cool or amas a huge horde of loot for their profile. It speaks volumes when that person is respected
across the server, sought after as a groupmate and considered the goto guy/girl on big raids when the guilds up against it.<P>

I've been lucky to meet several of these people in my time on RZ, and I really hope I meet them again.<P>

Thanks to these people, and thanks to the leaders of other guilds who would go the extra mile to keep things ticking over
on RZ and keep the focus on whats important. Thanks too to Ealill for taking over a guild at a _very_ tough time in EQ's
history. He kept the guild progressing in the face of a game run into the ground by its owners. I dont think I'd agree with
his absorbtion into <Hate> had I still been playing, but all good things must come to and end and the climate on Zek will be a whole new 
adventure for those who remain there.<P>

Lastly, when I killed my first few bats in Freeport and spotted a group of level 50's on their way to some place I'd 
never heard of...... the last thing I thought was that I'd be part of a guild as sucessful as Wudan. I'm glad we and other guilds
on RZ made our mark on the gaming world with the Sleeper kill. It sure wouldnt have been possible without the solid members
we've seen come and go. Thanks for your support.<P>

As for the future... Kad and I have just got back into gaming after waiting patiently for the European release of WOW. We'll 
hang with our RL friends.... keep in touch with the friends we made online and who knows where we'll end up :).

Peace<BR>
Needra Malkuth.<P>




